From 9b3afb3b56fc370bbcecba80da68a05125a57ead Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gigachad Enthusiast <32457258-AreteMaxxing@users.noreply.gitlab.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:20:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Graphics paging: keep plot builders, a switch per part,
 getCameraZoom argument

The game froze when the first city was founded with paging on. Of what
paging destroys, only the plot builder (bonus and improvement art) is never
destroyed by vanilla during a game: CvPlot::uninit alone destroys it, while
feature, route, yield and flag symbols and unit and city entities are
destroyed and remade in normal play. Plot builders now stay
(GRAPHICS_PAGING_PLOT_BUILDERS 0).

Paging is split into switches, all 1 except plot builders:
GRAPHICS_PAGING_UNITS, GRAPHICS_PAGING_CITIES, GRAPHICS_PAGING_PLOTS
(feature and route symbols), GRAPHICS_PAGING_PLOT_BUILDERS and the existing
GRAPHICS_PAGING_SYMBOLS. A plot remembers what its page-out removed; its
guards and its page-in cover only that.

CvGameInterface.getCameraZoom takes the argument list the game passes
(it failed with "takes no arguments (1 given)").

Serves: P11
---
